  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The killing of sons (127:14-21) is not drawn or glossed. The chiefs' claim is framed «وزاعمين أن ما جاء باطل وفساد». Musa: no motif; geometric for «إن الأرض لله», light for «عسى ربكم». STAGING v4: c1 (127): Pharaoh's court (palace, Egypt): the chiefs (three faceless men in dark robes) speak to Pharaoh (127:1); the camera is wide when Musa is named (127:7), as he is not in this scene; the gods of Pharaoh (127:13) are not drawn. Pharaoh answers (127:14); the killing of sons and the women (127:15-18) are never drawn: Pharaoh, the speaker, is held wide on the threat words (127:16, 127:18; no push-in on them), then in close-up with a crown plate for his boast of power (127:19-21). c2 (128-129): Musa (blue drop) and his people (Al-Muyassar: the Children of Israel; an uncountable group in light robes) in an Egyptian town by day. Musa speaks (128:1, 129:11); his commands (seek help, be patient) are not acted by the people, and the camera stays wide or in gentle pans with his drop in frame during his words; a geometric plate for the earth belongs to Allah (128:8-12). The people speak their complaint (129:1) with the camera on them; a seal plate for Musa's hope that is a promise (As-Sa'di: a promise Allah fulfilled, 129:12-19). Nothing of their persecution is drawn."
 },
